<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>

However, there's a small issue here. The `add` method shifts elements up starting from the specified index, so the element at the specified index after the insertion will be the newly added `role`. Therefore, the correct assertion should check the element at the specified index after the addition:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>

This assertion correctly states that if the index is within the valid range and the role is not null, then after adding the role at the specified index, the element at that index should be equal to the role.
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>
